WEBVTT


00:01:31.357 --> 00:01:32.491
No potty breaks.


00:01:32.958 --> 00:01:37.462
Dude, stop the truck.
You can leave us here. It's fine.


00:01:58.092 --> 00:01:59.760
Hey, how far is the lake?


00:02:00.257 --> 00:02:01.224
About a mile east.


00:02:01.658 --> 00:02:04.327
Perfect, because l need a bath.


00:02:20.424 --> 00:02:24.494
Not that l don't love this sexy,
impulsive thing, 'cause l do.


00:02:24.958 --> 00:02:27.827
But what are the chances
we're gonna get lost


00:02:27.925 --> 00:02:31.728
and, you know, we're gonna die horribly?


00:02:32.858 --> 00:02:36.895
Look, you keep talking like that
and you're gonna start lactating.


00:02:55.658 --> 00:02:57.926
Wow. It's so beautiful here.


00:03:01.058 --> 00:03:02.692
And real scary, huh?


00:03:03.458 --> 00:03:04.458
Okay, fine.


00:03:04.991 --> 00:03:06.692
Make fun of me.


00:03:06.791 --> 00:03:11.428
But when a Wolverine comes out
and mauls you, you're gonna be sorry.


00:03:12.391 --> 00:03:13.992
And you're naked.


00:03:14.591 --> 00:03:15.892
You noticed.


00:03:19.424 --> 00:03:20.458
God.


00:03:29.324 --> 00:03:30.758
What are you laughing at, pal?
l meant to do that.


00:03:35.124 --> 00:03:36.391
Come on.


00:03:36.491 --> 00:03:38.492
-You laughing at me?
-Yeah.


00:03:39.058 --> 00:03:40.592
Are you? l see.


00:03:44.291 --> 00:03:45.325
Hey, what's that?


00:03:45.791 --> 00:03:48.326
Come on, the water's cold. It shrinks a bit.


00:03:51.524 --> 00:03:53.626
What? l don't hear anything.


00:03:55.658 --> 00:03:59.094
-Hey, come on. l got an idea.
-Cool.


00:04:14.658 --> 00:04:15.925
God, something bit me.


00:04:16.257 --> 00:04:18.125
Yeah, right. Perhaps Wolverine.


00:04:25.191 --> 00:04:27.226
l've never heard you be so verbal.


00:04:28.191 --> 00:04:29.659
Take it easy, cowboy.


00:04:32.257 --> 00:04:34.559
Now, you see,
that's what l've been talking about.


00:04:39.458 --> 00:04:40.492
Help!


00:04:42.858 --> 00:04:43.858
Help!


00:04:47.891 --> 00:04:48.891
Oh, my God!


00:05:33.591 --> 00:05:35.993
Hey, big guy. You wanna come inside?


00:05:36.257 --> 00:05:37.324
Your mom needs some help.


00:05:37.458 --> 00:05:39.059
-Sure, Dad.
-Okay.


00:05:51.891 --> 00:05:53.025
Sadie!


00:06:17.025 --> 00:06:20.695
No cell phone reception.
It's like we've gone back in time.


00:06:21.991 --> 00:06:25.594
How can this place smell of cookies
and foot cream simultaneously?


00:06:26.224 --> 00:06:28.659
Well, they were
two of Aunt Sadie's favorite things.


00:06:28.791 --> 00:06:30.792
That and dropping F-bombs.


00:06:32.025 --> 00:06:34.727
l am not gonna miss that at Thanksgiving.


00:06:34.825 --> 00:06:37.794
-Didn't she always blame it on the dog?
-Yeah.


00:06:38.991 --> 00:06:44.262
You know, as both your wife
and your real estate agent,


00:06:45.424 --> 00:06:50.295
l can pretty much say with confidence
that most of this crap has gotta go.


00:06:54.058 --> 00:06:55.759
lt's gonna be a huge job.


00:06:55.858 --> 00:06:59.161
Yeah, but we can't bring it all back
to the house.


00:07:01.791 --> 00:07:03.125
She was eccentric.


00:07:03.858 --> 00:07:05.059
Really?


00:07:05.624 --> 00:07:08.560
Yeah, a different word
popped into my mind.


00:07:12.025 --> 00:07:15.261
You know, everything's almost exactly
how l remember it.


00:07:15.357 --> 00:07:17.325
l mean, l never thought that...


00:07:17.691 --> 00:07:20.026
Well, l never thought
that we'd be cleaning out her cabin, so...


00:07:22.357 --> 00:07:25.460
l feel like l'm selling part of my childhood
with this place.


00:07:25.558 --> 00:07:28.627
l know, honey. But it's best we stay in town.


00:07:30.891 --> 00:07:32.425
-Can l have that?
-No.


00:07:35.391 --> 00:07:36.492
-Yeah, sure.
-No.


00:07:36.624 --> 00:07:37.591
-Yeah.
-Yes.


00:07:44.191 --> 00:07:48.495
l have a pop quiz for you,
Mr. EPA Scientist. Okay?


00:07:49.058 --> 00:07:53.162
So what kind of animal
lives in a tank like that one?


00:07:55.825 --> 00:07:57.159
The smart money's on that lizard right there.


00:07:57.257 --> 00:07:58.558
-What?
-ls there nothing there?


00:07:58.658 --> 00:08:00.126
Well, that was probably my mistake,
l thought it was...


00:08:00.558 --> 00:08:01.825
Funny!


00:08:01.925 --> 00:08:03.660
Freak out the city girl.


00:08:03.758 --> 00:08:06.427
Just 'cause l don't share
the Bickerman infatuation with...


00:08:06.524 --> 00:08:09.226
What? Life? Nature?


00:08:09.324 --> 00:08:12.126
Nature to you. Disgusting creatures to me.


00:08:12.925 --> 00:08:14.359
All right, well, heads up for both of you,


00:08:14.458 --> 00:08:17.093
there might be an escaped lizard
somewhere in the house.


00:08:17.191 --> 00:08:18.825
Can we keep it?


00:08:18.925 --> 00:08:22.361
Absolutely not. No.
Besides, you already have a pet.


00:08:22.458 --> 00:08:23.792
Crocodiles aren't pets.


00:08:23.891 --> 00:08:24.992
Well, they are to some people, pal.


00:08:25.257 --> 00:08:26.291
Not if they're stuffed.


00:08:26.424 --> 00:08:27.458
You know what?


00:08:27.858 --> 00:08:32.596
lf we find any kind of vermin in the house,
your dad is gonna take care of it.


00:08:34.558 --> 00:08:35.592
Dad?


00:08:35.691 --> 00:08:38.994
ln a completely humane way, of course.


00:08:39.324 --> 00:08:40.458
Sure. Sit down.


00:09:01.424 --> 00:09:04.593
-Mr. Bickerman?
-Hey, Nate. Nathan. Come on in.


00:09:09.391 --> 00:09:10.425
Sheriff Willinger.


00:09:10.524 --> 00:09:12.125
-Hey. Susan.
-Hey.


00:09:12.224 --> 00:09:13.858
lt's been a while.


00:09:14.058 --> 00:09:16.160
Almost a year since Sadie passed.


00:09:16.257 --> 00:09:17.524
l was going by, l saw your vehicle.


00:09:17.858 --> 00:09:19.793
l thought l'd drop in and say hey.


00:09:19.891 --> 00:09:20.992
-Yeah, of course.
-Yeah.


00:09:21.925 --> 00:09:22.959
Takes after Sadie, huh?


00:09:24.458 --> 00:09:27.527
Connor, could you give us a minute, please?


00:09:27.791 --> 00:09:29.192
-Okay.
-Thanks.


00:09:31.025 --> 00:09:33.293
Yeah, we haven't told him, so...


00:09:36.858 --> 00:09:37.858
l don't blame you.


00:09:37.958 --> 00:09:40.527
A boy his age, that would raise questions
you don't have answers to.


00:09:41.658 --> 00:09:44.227
Hell, l'd like to know what your aunt
was doing feeding wild crocs.


00:09:44.758 --> 00:09:47.327
Well, she was lonely.


00:09:48.324 --> 00:09:49.925
l mean, l know we live in town.


00:09:50.025 --> 00:09:52.127
We don't get out here that much. And with...


00:09:52.224 --> 00:09:54.059
You know, ever since Connor was born,
and our jobs, it's...


00:09:54.157 --> 00:09:55.224
Well, there's never enough time.


00:09:56.224 --> 00:09:57.858
And now the place is for sale.


00:09:59.791 --> 00:10:03.728
lt took a year for us to drive out here
to clean up Sadie's stuff. It's...


00:10:03.825 --> 00:10:06.994
You know, believe me,
this isn't easy for me. We...


00:10:07.092 --> 00:10:09.761
lf we had a choice,
we probably wouldn't even sell it.


00:10:09.858 --> 00:10:12.927
Yeah, but it's not like we can come out here
and have a picnic


00:10:13.025 --> 00:10:14.159
and forget about what happened.


00:10:14.257 --> 00:10:16.926
l don't even like bringing Connor here
for a few hours.


00:10:17.324 --> 00:10:19.559
Well, that's understandable.


00:10:19.658 --> 00:10:23.661
l'd like you to know
that l've been all over that lake.


00:10:23.758 --> 00:10:26.827
Back to front, top to bottom,
had a sonar rig brought in.


00:10:26.925 --> 00:10:30.495
l can tell you, ma'am, there ain't nothing
swimming in that lake bigger than a trout.


00:10:30.591 --> 00:10:32.459
Yeah, but you can never be sure.


00:10:32.558 --> 00:10:36.862
-Right?
-Ma'am, when my predecessor left the job,


00:10:36.958 --> 00:10:38.959
-the county wanted to hire somebody...
-Hey, where are you going?


00:10:39.058 --> 00:10:40.692
...who could guarantee
that what happened here


00:10:40.791 --> 00:10:42.392
didn't happen again, and that's me.


00:10:42.491 --> 00:10:43.859
Now, you're gonna have to trust me.


00:10:44.791 --> 00:10:47.860
You know? l've seen things that are
a lot worse than what happened here.


00:10:47.958 --> 00:10:52.095
Hell, l had a 6'5'' cross-dresser
come at me with a machete.


00:10:55.691 --> 00:10:57.526
What l'm trying to say is,


00:10:58.424 --> 00:11:01.994
in this world it's the people
you gotta worry about, not the animals.


00:11:02.291 --> 00:11:04.059
-l'm gonna be on my way, here.
-Sure, sure.


00:11:04.157 --> 00:11:05.191
Thank you for coming by.


00:11:06.691 --> 00:11:08.325
You take care, now.


00:11:29.357 --> 00:11:33.060
All l'm saying is that if the lake is cleared,
there's no reason to sell.


00:11:33.157 --> 00:11:36.260
Nathan, we didn't even come here
when Sadie was alive.


00:11:36.357 --> 00:11:40.094
l know. But, l mean, no one knows better
than you how bad the market is right now.


00:11:40.191 --> 00:11:42.393
l'm just saying, why don't we wait?


00:11:42.491 --> 00:11:44.860
You know, test it out. We could... Please?


00:11:46.958 --> 00:11:50.361
You know what? Fine. Okay.
We can wait until the market recovers.


00:11:50.458 --> 00:11:53.227
-But Connor is not swimming in that lake.
-Done.


00:11:53.324 --> 00:11:54.291
But he's not gonna make any friends


00:11:54.391 --> 00:11:56.659
if we keep dragging him off
to the middle of nowhere.


00:11:56.791 --> 00:11:57.825
Well...


00:11:58.025 --> 00:11:59.192
Connor?


00:12:01.058 --> 00:12:03.226
-Where'd he go?
-l don't know.


00:12:05.491 --> 00:12:08.460
Come here, little guy.
l'm not gonna hurt you.


00:12:40.224 --> 00:12:43.293
Looks like l got a pet after all. Lots of them.


00:12:45.958 --> 00:12:48.493
Connor! Don't run off
without telling us, okay?


00:12:48.591 --> 00:12:50.159
-Sorry.
-Come on.


00:12:50.257 --> 00:12:52.292
We're driving back to town.


00:13:11.157 --> 00:13:12.992
lt's 6:00 a.m. and you're not on the trail.


00:13:13.092 --> 00:13:15.294
-You going soft on me?
-Yeah.


00:13:15.391 --> 00:13:17.860
-l thought you had a big day.
-l do.


00:13:19.124 --> 00:13:21.826
Don't l at least get a ''good morning''?


00:13:21.958 --> 00:13:24.560
Sorry. We lost another one.


00:13:25.958 --> 00:13:28.360
The signal from the elk's radio collar
went and became erratic,


00:13:28.458 --> 00:13:31.494
and then we lost it completely
yesterday afternoon, so...


00:13:31.591 --> 00:13:33.192
This one is gonna be the last one.


00:13:33.291 --> 00:13:35.426
Meaning you know
what's been happening to them?


00:13:35.524 --> 00:13:36.625
l think it's a poacher.


00:13:37.357 --> 00:13:40.259
l think they're bringing hunters
onto state land. l think it's a business.


00:13:40.357 --> 00:13:41.491
And...


00:13:44.691 --> 00:13:47.060
l hope you find your bad guy.


00:13:49.058 --> 00:13:50.092
Good morning.


00:13:50.191 --> 00:13:54.061
And don't forget to say goodbye
to your zoologist-in-training.


00:13:54.157 --> 00:13:57.026
Right. Right. Hey, is Vica coming by today?


00:13:58.124 --> 00:13:59.859
She has to take her dog to the vet.


00:13:59.958 --> 00:14:02.093
Something about
it having another panic attack,


00:14:02.191 --> 00:14:05.961
but l promised Connor
l would spend the day with him anyway, so...


00:14:06.058 --> 00:14:08.593
Hey, Connor, l'm heading out the door.


00:14:08.691 --> 00:14:12.027
You wanna say goodbye to me
before l leave? Love you.


00:14:12.791 --> 00:14:16.694
-Goodbye? When did you get back?
-Late last night. Something came up at work


00:14:16.825 --> 00:14:20.028
and l will tell you all about it
when l get home, okay?


00:14:20.124 --> 00:14:22.526
-But, Dad...
-Hey, l got to go, okay?


00:14:24.624 --> 00:14:25.658
Bye.


00:14:59.458 --> 00:15:03.562
God! Mother of...
Next year, you are going to summer school.


00:15:04.558 --> 00:15:08.428
You've been on there all morning.
When are you gonna be done?


00:15:08.524 --> 00:15:11.226
Soon, honey. There are a lot of cabins
that need renting


00:15:11.324 --> 00:15:14.093
and l have so many people counting on me.


00:15:17.357 --> 00:15:19.726
Two hours, tops, okay? l promise.


00:15:23.324 --> 00:15:26.126
Honey, why don't you just go play outside?


00:15:27.558 --> 00:15:28.725
Connor?


00:15:44.724 --> 00:15:45.791
Hey, guys.


00:15:47.025 --> 00:15:48.793
Hey, guys.
Do you wanna see something cool?


00:15:49.724 --> 00:15:52.560
''Hey, guys. Wanna see something cool?''


00:15:55.925 --> 00:15:58.894
-What a freaking jester.
-What a dork.


00:16:11.224 --> 00:16:12.658
Feeding time.


00:16:40.724 --> 00:16:41.791
That's all l got.


00:16:44.858 --> 00:16:46.759
Hey, no eating the cook.


00:16:47.458 --> 00:16:49.126
l'll try to bring more next time.


00:17:08.357 --> 00:17:09.725
Where is it?


00:17:10.524 --> 00:17:13.393
Around back. Tried to take a chunk
out of one of my customers.


00:17:13.491 --> 00:17:15.426
lt's wicked big.


00:17:21.124 --> 00:17:22.959
l think he came up through the toilet.


00:17:33.058 --> 00:17:34.926
You're wasting my time.


00:17:35.825 --> 00:17:37.226
Take it easy, Tony.


00:17:40.157 --> 00:17:41.424
Willinger.


00:17:43.491 --> 00:17:44.792
Yes, dear.


00:17:47.958 --> 00:17:49.793
Yes, dear. Yeah. Yeah.


00:17:51.157 --> 00:17:53.425
Here, could you hold on? Hold on, dear.


00:17:54.724 --> 00:17:56.025
Willinger.


00:17:56.357 --> 00:17:57.958
l got a lead on my missing elk.


00:17:58.058 --> 00:18:00.326
Seems she's wandering around
somewhere near Sadie's lake.


00:18:00.724 --> 00:18:03.159
Nathan, l don't wanna hear anything
about crocodiles.


00:18:03.257 --> 00:18:07.194
There's nothing in that lake
bigger than a trout. Just stay put.


00:18:10.058 --> 00:18:11.859
That was productive.


00:18:13.058 --> 00:18:14.359
Yes, dear.


00:18:18.357 --> 00:18:20.158
Well, you shouldn't have put it
in the microwave.


00:18:41.491 --> 00:18:42.959
I wish I could believe you.


00:18:43.758 --> 00:18:46.093
lt was a one-night stand, Marsha.
She meant nothing to me.


00:18:46.191 --> 00:18:47.992
-l have absolutely no feelings for her.
-But this is how...


00:18:48.092 --> 00:18:50.894
He was kissing Jessica
before the last commercial.


00:18:50.991 --> 00:18:54.794
...Susan's little one? The little one
with the same hair and eyes as yours.


00:18:55.058 --> 00:18:58.327
Susan? Susan means
absolutely nothing to me.


00:18:59.058 --> 00:19:00.526
Where's my mom?


00:19:00.624 --> 00:19:02.092
Connor, where have you been?


00:19:02.191 --> 00:19:03.292
Forgot my phone.


00:19:04.424 --> 00:19:05.858
Where are you going?


00:19:05.958 --> 00:19:09.928
Honey, l am so sorry, but l have a thing.


00:19:13.658 --> 00:19:14.925
What was l saying?


00:19:15.025 --> 00:19:16.693
l have a last minute open house.


00:19:17.724 --> 00:19:20.259
So l am gonna leave you with Vica
for the rest of the day


00:19:20.357 --> 00:19:22.726
and tomorrow we will go see a movie.
l promise.


00:19:22.825 --> 00:19:23.792
But you said that we'd...


00:19:23.891 --> 00:19:25.759
Connor, this is important.
Please understand.


00:19:25.891 --> 00:19:27.525
But l need to show you something.


00:19:27.925 --> 00:19:28.959
Well, show me when l get home,


00:19:29.991 --> 00:19:31.559
l love you so much.


00:19:31.658 --> 00:19:32.692
Bye.


00:19:52.491 --> 00:19:54.292
Connor! What are you doing?


00:19:54.958 --> 00:19:58.628
You smell like dead goat. Go take bath.


00:19:59.191 --> 00:20:03.395
l'm going to the store
to get some baseball cards.


00:20:04.491 --> 00:20:06.659
l don't care about your baseball cards.


00:20:17.424 --> 00:20:19.993
Connor! You didn't take bath.


00:21:22.092 --> 00:21:24.093
You got to stay away
from those cookies, boy.


00:21:24.825 --> 00:21:28.395
You seem to have gained
quite a bit of weight since l last saw you.


00:21:28.591 --> 00:21:30.960
About two minutes ago.


00:21:31.191 --> 00:21:32.325
Well, l...


00:21:33.291 --> 00:21:35.726
lf it were me, l'd kick your little butt.


00:21:36.891 --> 00:21:40.027
Parents' number.
And not the fake one, either.


00:21:44.025 --> 00:21:46.193
Gotta be out here somewhere.


00:21:54.991 --> 00:21:55.991
God!


00:21:56.092 --> 00:21:57.359
Sorry. Sorry.


00:21:57.624 --> 00:22:00.360
Thanks. l think you knocked out a filling.


00:22:00.458 --> 00:22:03.160
Well, l know the name of a good dentist
in town, if you need one.


00:22:03.257 --> 00:22:06.593
Thanks for the tip.
Maybe we can call it with your space phone.


00:22:07.991 --> 00:22:11.728
Space phone? Yeah, good one.
No, it's a radar antenna. Are you okay?


00:22:12.524 --> 00:22:13.758
Yeah, l'll let you know.


00:22:14.424 --> 00:22:17.960
l'm a zoologist.
l'm doing a project for the EPA on elk, so.


00:22:18.357 --> 00:22:21.927
Elk? Like deer with big antlers?


00:22:22.491 --> 00:22:24.526
Yeah, but don't tell the deer that.


00:22:33.624 --> 00:22:36.493
-Seriously, Connor? Stealing meat?
-No, l...


00:22:39.291 --> 00:22:44.162
Mr. Dimitri, l am so sorry.
He's never done anything like this before.


00:22:44.591 --> 00:22:45.758
Really?


00:22:47.591 --> 00:22:52.062
Yeah, he just loves meat.
Ever since he was wee high...


00:22:52.458 --> 00:22:53.559
Well, goody-goody for him.


00:22:54.391 --> 00:22:57.026
All he has to do now is pay for it.


00:22:57.124 --> 00:22:58.925
Nobody wants to buy used meat.


00:22:59.257 --> 00:23:00.291
No, of course.


00:23:00.558 --> 00:23:01.859
-lt's not for me, it's for...
-Connor,


00:23:02.724 --> 00:23:04.559
l want you to go straight home
and wait for me in your room.


00:23:05.791 --> 00:23:07.192
-But, Mom...
-Now.


00:23:12.257 --> 00:23:16.394
Look, l promise this will never happen again.


00:23:17.524 --> 00:23:19.158
He's a good kid, really. He's just...


00:23:20.691 --> 00:23:21.758
He's a little bored,


00:23:22.558 --> 00:23:24.493
and that is my fault, not his.


00:23:25.891 --> 00:23:28.693
So, how much do l owe you?


00:23:29.658 --> 00:23:33.261
Just to let you know,
the chicken went off sale yesterday.


00:23:33.891 --> 00:23:36.793
So, are they usually like that?


00:23:37.624 --> 00:23:40.626
Well, unless there's a species
of flying-elk-head l haven't heard of,


00:23:40.724 --> 00:23:42.559
l'm gonna go out on a limb and say no.


00:23:45.092 --> 00:23:46.693
Sorry. Excuse me.


00:23:50.825 --> 00:23:51.959
-Hello.
-Hey.


00:23:52.791 --> 00:23:54.893
l just got pulled away
from one of the biggest commissions


00:23:55.224 --> 00:23:58.827
of my life to bail your son from Dimitri's,


00:23:58.925 --> 00:24:01.527
where he was being held for shoplifting.


00:24:02.357 --> 00:24:08.596
Shoplifting? Okay, tell Dimitri
we'll pay for whatever candy bar he stole.


00:24:08.691 --> 00:24:12.227
l paid for it, honey, but it wasn't candy.


00:24:13.324 --> 00:24:15.592
No, he had a backpack full of meat.


00:24:16.257 --> 00:24:17.324
He's stealing meat?


00:24:17.624 --> 00:24:22.362
Yeah. And apparently,
he's taken up smoking.


00:24:23.025 --> 00:24:24.059
Smoking?


00:24:25.291 --> 00:24:28.027
So, remind me to put a lock
on the wine cabinet.


00:24:28.758 --> 00:24:31.393
He said they're Vica's
but she doesn't even smoke.


00:24:32.092 --> 00:24:33.359
And speaking of Vica,


00:24:33.458 --> 00:24:35.793
why are we paying her to sit at home
and watch TV


00:24:35.891 --> 00:24:37.792
whilst Connor is out shoplifting?


00:24:37.891 --> 00:24:40.126
Well, at least we're keeping one of them
off the street.


00:24:41.124 --> 00:24:44.560
Did we not feed Connor the right things
as a baby?


00:24:44.658 --> 00:24:47.427
Did l eat too much chili
when he was in my womb,


00:24:47.524 --> 00:24:49.392
and now he's a sociopath?


00:24:49.491 --> 00:24:51.492
What? He's not a sociopath.


00:24:51.591 --> 00:24:53.225
l mean, every kid does something like this
at some point.


00:24:53.324 --> 00:24:54.825
He's just... He's being a little boy.


00:24:54.925 --> 00:24:57.060
A little boy who's been unsupervised.


00:24:57.524 --> 00:24:59.392
Okay, put him on the phone,
l wanna talk to him.


00:25:00.858 --> 00:25:01.892
l sent him home.


00:25:02.658 --> 00:25:06.661
Sorry about your day. For what it's worth,
mine isn't going much better.


00:25:06.791 --> 00:25:12.029
Really? Sorry.
Okay, well, l'll see you at home.


00:25:12.124 --> 00:25:13.625
Okay. Bye, babe.


00:25:13.724 --> 00:25:17.961
Yeah. And l just hope you don't become
a vegetarian any time soon.


00:25:18.257 --> 00:25:19.691
l'm voting for pork chops.


00:25:20.391 --> 00:25:21.425
Bye.


00:25:26.991 --> 00:25:30.561
Sorry about that. Cell reception out here
is a once in a lifetime opportunity, so...


00:25:30.658 --> 00:25:33.260
Hey, what could have eaten the body?
A bear?


00:25:33.558 --> 00:25:35.860
l told you, l saw cougar tracks over there.


00:25:36.058 --> 00:25:38.493
He wasn't asking you, Charlie.
He was asking the zookeeper.


00:25:38.591 --> 00:25:39.625
Zoologist.


00:25:39.925 --> 00:25:42.027
-lsn't that what l said?
-No.


00:25:42.791 --> 00:25:46.227
l don't think it was a bear
but it may have been a coug'ar.


00:25:46.925 --> 00:25:48.126
What did l say?


00:25:48.424 --> 00:25:50.058
A cougar named Reba.


00:25:53.524 --> 00:25:55.759
-You know what you did?
-Yeah.


00:26:06.092 --> 00:26:08.427
Excuse me, sugar, could you pick that up?


00:26:13.291 --> 00:26:15.326
Thank you, handsome. You can keep it.


00:26:21.124 --> 00:26:23.893
Why would a hunter chop off the head?


00:26:23.991 --> 00:26:25.859
Yeah, isn't the head
supposed to be the best part?


00:26:26.391 --> 00:26:31.129
Well, that's what l keep trying to tell you,
but you don't wanna go for it.


00:26:33.558 --> 00:26:36.394
Well, it doesn't make rational sense, no.
But that might be the point.


00:26:36.491 --> 00:26:37.558
She might be trying to mess with me.


00:26:38.624 --> 00:26:39.725
Hunters are weird.


00:26:40.391 --> 00:26:41.458
Yes.


00:26:41.691 --> 00:26:45.061
So if it wasn't this cougar lady,
then what was it?


00:26:45.624 --> 00:26:47.058
l don't know.


00:26:48.025 --> 00:26:49.526
Look, if you guys run into any trouble,


00:26:49.624 --> 00:26:51.659
there's a cabin
just on the other side of that point.


00:26:51.758 --> 00:26:54.460
You can duck in there if you'd like, okay?


00:26:54.558 --> 00:26:56.226
Yeah, what kind of trouble?


00:26:56.558 --> 00:26:59.560
Just be safe and don't mess with the elk.


00:27:01.291 --> 00:27:02.892
All right? Sorry.


00:27:04.092 --> 00:27:06.794
-l hope you find your moose killer.
-Elk!


00:27:07.324 --> 00:27:08.391
Whatever.


00:27:08.691 --> 00:27:11.760
Excuse me,
is there a Reba around here anywhere?


00:27:12.558 --> 00:27:14.259
Just there? Thanks.


00:27:16.291 --> 00:27:17.325
Excuse me.


00:27:17.724 --> 00:27:20.093
-You Reba?
-Depends on who's asking.


00:27:20.624 --> 00:27:21.858
l contacted you, l'm Brett.


00:27:23.424 --> 00:27:25.192
Then that would make me Reba. Have a seat.


00:27:32.391 --> 00:27:37.829
Now, if l may say so, that photo in your ad,
it just don't do you no justice, Reba.


00:27:38.958 --> 00:27:40.826
Now, my good buddy Walt here and myself,


00:27:41.825 --> 00:27:45.195
we thought we were just getting ourselves
a hunting guide,


00:27:45.291 --> 00:27:49.261
but, girl, you are one fine package.


00:27:50.691 --> 00:27:54.227
Well, aren't you just such a sweet talker.


00:27:58.025 --> 00:28:02.662
Once we're miles away from civilization,
been out there a few days,


00:28:02.758 --> 00:28:06.495
missed everything you shot at,
and your belly starts grumbling,


00:28:06.591 --> 00:28:11.796
you're gonna appreciate my aim
a lot more than my other assets.


00:28:12.124 --> 00:28:13.391
lf you receive my meaning.


00:28:14.791 --> 00:28:18.995
Well, l, for one, am a multi-tasker
and l plan on appreciating both.


00:28:23.025 --> 00:28:24.059
So,


00:28:25.624 --> 00:28:28.660
Brett, was it? How'd you hear about Reba?


00:28:30.224 --> 00:28:31.258
lnternet.


00:28:32.291 --> 00:28:33.525
lnternet.


00:28:36.424 --> 00:28:38.692
How about you two load your gear
into my truck?


00:28:38.791 --> 00:28:40.893
lt's the big one out front.


00:28:40.991 --> 00:28:43.493
Boat on the back, gun rack up front,


00:28:44.224 --> 00:28:48.261
mildly offensive bumper-sticker. You'll see.


00:28:48.458 --> 00:28:50.760
All right. Let's go, Walt.


00:28:50.925 --> 00:28:51.925
Hey, hey, hey, hey.


00:28:54.558 --> 00:28:56.426
All right. There.


00:28:58.724 --> 00:28:59.858
Thank you.


00:29:04.025 --> 00:29:05.393
So, Brett?


00:29:07.324 --> 00:29:09.793
You play your cards pretty close to the vest,


00:29:12.025 --> 00:29:14.460
but l think l deserve to know
what you're really doing here.


00:29:15.724 --> 00:29:16.724
Your website said that...


00:29:17.257 --> 00:29:19.092
l don't have a website.


00:29:24.591 --> 00:29:27.694
Well, let's just say you're kind of a legend.


00:29:29.558 --> 00:29:30.792
A legend?


00:29:31.691 --> 00:29:33.125
Of what sort?


00:29:33.224 --> 00:29:35.726
Bigfoot? Crop circles?


00:29:36.458 --> 00:29:37.492
Global warming?


00:29:37.591 --> 00:29:41.394
No. You know how to find things
that don't wanna be found.


00:29:43.524 --> 00:29:45.058
l'm looking for a girl.


00:29:46.257 --> 00:29:48.492
A girl that hangs out in the woods?


00:29:49.191 --> 00:29:51.426
Or the lake. l'm not really sure.


00:29:54.324 --> 00:29:56.893
All right, look. l don't have a chance
of finding her on my own,


00:29:56.991 --> 00:29:58.959
and you're the only guide
that goes into the area.


00:30:02.424 --> 00:30:03.925
All right, then.


00:30:05.124 --> 00:30:10.262
Elks for the yahoos.
One Lois Lane for Superman here.


00:30:27.324 --> 00:30:28.324
Where is it?


00:30:38.391 --> 00:30:39.558
The meat stealer.


00:30:40.591 --> 00:30:42.326
Your mother called. Go to room.


00:30:42.491 --> 00:30:44.826
-Lost something? Like a lighter?
-Give it back.


00:30:46.724 --> 00:30:48.025
You tried to get me in trouble


00:30:48.124 --> 00:30:50.192
by putting this and the cigarettes
in my backpack.


00:30:50.558 --> 00:30:51.825
Give it back right now.


00:30:52.458 --> 00:30:54.626
And you can ask my mom
for the cigarettes.


00:31:00.257 --> 00:31:02.292
Teddy? Teddy?


00:31:24.324 --> 00:31:28.528
Connor! Come back here.
Your mother will be mad at me.


00:31:49.257 --> 00:31:51.459
Devil child, where did you go?


00:32:24.424 --> 00:32:28.494
Okay, so l'm down to one hotdog.
You guys are gonna have to share.


00:32:33.391 --> 00:32:34.558
Connor!


00:32:39.157 --> 00:32:40.525
lt was here.


00:32:45.691 --> 00:32:49.461
Nathan, l am sick and tired
of these false alarms and pranks.


00:32:50.624 --> 00:32:53.259
Now, l drove all the way out here
because you promised me a bloody mess.


00:32:53.357 --> 00:32:56.560
-Now, where is it?
-lt was right here.


00:33:01.291 --> 00:33:02.925
Teddy, stay.


00:33:03.357 --> 00:33:04.958
Come on, Teddy, get away from there.


00:33:11.391 --> 00:33:12.391
Wait.


00:33:17.092 --> 00:33:18.393
Teddy, no.


00:33:19.092 --> 00:33:20.092
Watch yourself.


00:33:22.724 --> 00:33:24.992
Teddy, no! Come back, Teddy. No.


00:33:39.858 --> 00:33:40.959
lt's a stick.


00:33:41.324 --> 00:33:42.391
Yeah.


00:33:43.925 --> 00:33:46.627
Poor Teddy,
now l know why you have a panic attack.


00:33:58.958 --> 00:34:01.293
-How many elk did you say you've lost?
-ln the last six months?


00:34:01.491 --> 00:34:02.491
Yeah.


00:34:03.058 --> 00:34:05.393
Too many.
l'm starting to think it's not a poacher.


00:34:06.357 --> 00:34:10.227
Hey, l checked that lake three times.


00:34:10.591 --> 00:34:14.127
And, Nathan, l swear to God
my eyes were open the whole time.


00:34:14.224 --> 00:34:16.859
Now look, l may be from the city,
but l know my way around the wilderness.


00:34:17.324 --> 00:34:21.061
Last time you checked that lake was a year
and a half ago, and things change.


00:34:21.157 --> 00:34:23.759
Now, we owe it to the community
to make sure that lake is clear.


00:34:23.858 --> 00:34:26.694
l don't live with my head in the sand.
l need evidence.


00:34:27.291 --> 00:34:28.458
Well, what if something just came
and ate it?


00:34:29.025 --> 00:34:31.794
And what if the evidence is a stick?


00:34:32.825 --> 00:34:35.561
l don't have sophisticated sonar equipment.


00:34:35.691 --> 00:34:38.260
We'd have to order it in.
That would take days.


00:34:40.124 --> 00:34:41.158
Okay.


00:34:42.791 --> 00:34:45.760
But we do have the next best thing
back at the station.


00:34:47.191 --> 00:34:48.559
Well, great.


00:34:49.357 --> 00:34:51.692
So you and l, we'll go back,
we'll come here, we'll check the lake.


00:34:51.791 --> 00:34:54.293
Now, nothing would make me happier
than for you to be right.


00:34:54.958 --> 00:34:57.627
All right. All right, let's go fishing.


00:35:22.958 --> 00:35:24.259
Yes, dear.


00:35:24.958 --> 00:35:27.460
Yes, dear. Why don't you do that?


00:35:30.424 --> 00:35:32.726
l bought this with my own money.


00:35:33.391 --> 00:35:36.660
You know, in New York City we got people
who swear they've seen Elvis


00:35:36.758 --> 00:35:38.659
at 63rd and Park.


00:35:38.758 --> 00:35:41.427
We got people
who swear they've been abducted by aliens


00:35:41.524 --> 00:35:45.594
and, yes, we've even got people
who swear they've seen albino crocodiles


00:35:45.958 --> 00:35:47.259
-in the subway.
-Sheriff!


00:35:47.357 --> 00:35:48.424
Shut up!


00:36:00.558 --> 00:36:04.628
Wow! That's a little much
for Aroostook County, don't you think?


00:36:05.191 --> 00:36:10.195
l believe a boy scout
should always be prepared.


00:36:11.624 --> 00:36:13.292
Especially one from Jersey.


00:36:13.391 --> 00:36:14.558
Connor?


00:36:21.458 --> 00:36:22.525
Vica?


00:36:25.925 --> 00:36:27.092
Connor!


00:36:45.691 --> 00:36:49.428
l think the sun is better over here.


00:37:22.925 --> 00:37:25.994
Connor? Connor, are you here?


00:37:27.825 --> 00:37:30.527
You know, l told you to go straight home.


00:37:31.058 --> 00:37:32.225
Connor!


00:37:34.157 --> 00:37:35.157
Mom,


00:37:36.257 --> 00:37:37.591
l think l did something bad.


00:37:37.691 --> 00:37:40.060
-Sweetie, is that blood?
-No, no, no.


00:37:40.157 --> 00:37:42.359
-What is...
-lt's not my blood. It's...


00:37:43.291 --> 00:37:44.425
l was by the lake...


00:37:56.758 --> 00:37:59.460
ln the water. He's in the water!


00:38:15.191 --> 00:38:16.191
You coming, Ellie?


00:38:16.858 --> 00:38:17.892
lsn't it a little cold?


00:38:19.092 --> 00:38:20.426
That's why we came out here.


00:38:20.658 --> 00:38:23.594
Get out into the real world,
the way things used to be.


00:38:24.257 --> 00:38:27.126
You know, when our ancestors came here,
there were no heated pools.


00:38:27.691 --> 00:38:30.393
There didn't have iPods either,
but l noticed you brought yours.


00:38:30.791 --> 00:38:33.093
Hey, at least you got away
from he-who-must-not-be-named.


00:38:33.191 --> 00:38:34.825
Yeah, let's not talk about it, okay?


00:38:35.224 --> 00:38:37.926
l bought a new bikini for this trip,
so l have to use it,


00:38:38.025 --> 00:38:39.793
whether the water is freezing or not.


00:38:40.791 --> 00:38:41.858
See, now she's got the right idea.


00:38:43.491 --> 00:38:45.659
Or, l have a better idea.


00:38:46.224 --> 00:38:48.292
Why don't we all just jump in naked?


00:38:48.391 --> 00:38:50.459
That'd be hilarious, right?


00:38:51.624 --> 00:38:52.958
You guys first.


00:38:57.092 --> 00:38:58.059
lt worked!


00:38:58.825 --> 00:39:01.394
Yeah, l guess the image of you naked
really did the trick.


00:39:14.257 --> 00:39:16.225
He actually thought
we were gonna jump in there naked.


00:39:16.324 --> 00:39:17.625
l know. He is so...


00:39:17.724 --> 00:39:19.725
-Obnoxious, right?
-l was gonna say funny.


00:39:20.558 --> 00:39:21.592
You're kidding.


00:39:21.691 --> 00:39:23.893
Not like ''l'm gonna sleep with him'' funny,


00:39:23.991 --> 00:39:26.593
but like, ''l'd set him up
with one of my fat friends'' funny.


00:39:26.724 --> 00:39:29.026
Like you have any fat friends.


00:39:29.124 --> 00:39:31.626
-Clarissa put on a ton of weight recently.
-Tara!


00:39:31.991 --> 00:39:35.027
-What?
-She's pregnant, not fat.


00:39:35.458 --> 00:39:39.461
lt's not all baby. She's not giving birth
to, like, Andre the freaking Giant.


00:39:39.624 --> 00:39:40.891
You're terrible.


00:39:41.558 --> 00:39:43.660
Just being realistic.


00:39:46.324 --> 00:39:47.658
That's a really cute bikini.


00:39:47.758 --> 00:39:49.059
-Where'd you get that?
-Thanks. Clarissa's closet.


00:39:49.391 --> 00:39:50.692
Have you heard from Brett?


00:39:50.791 --> 00:39:52.826
,
No, if l wanted to talk to Brett
l would have called him, so...


00:39:53.257 --> 00:39:54.958
Well, you're not gonna let him apologize?


00:39:55.058 --> 00:39:57.927
l'm gonna let him stew for a few days,
or weeks. l haven't decided.


00:39:58.391 --> 00:39:59.425
Would you?


00:39:59.858 --> 00:40:01.059
Does he know about you and Aaron?


00:40:01.257 --> 00:40:02.291
What?


00:40:02.391 --> 00:40:04.493
No, there's nothing to know.


00:40:04.591 --> 00:40:08.027
Yeah, and l'm not gonna hook up
with the lacrosse team.


00:40:08.458 --> 00:40:10.293
-Seriously, there's nothing.
-Yeah, right.


00:40:10.658 --> 00:40:11.692
Honest.


00:40:12.691 --> 00:40:13.725
You ready?


00:40:13.825 --> 00:40:16.327
-Yeah, let's go.
-lt's gonna be cold.


00:40:30.524 --> 00:40:31.958
Oh, God.


00:40:38.658 --> 00:40:39.992
Oh, my God!


00:40:52.424 --> 00:40:54.192
lt's good though, eh?


00:41:06.624 --> 00:41:09.927
-What's going on?
-l can't get through to my wife.


00:41:10.157 --> 00:41:13.260
l haven't been able to get through to mine
since '86.


00:41:16.424 --> 00:41:18.225
Connor, try 911 again.


00:41:21.591 --> 00:41:22.858
lt won't go through.


00:41:23.891 --> 00:41:25.192
Vica? Vica? Hold still, honey.


00:41:25.391 --> 00:41:27.126
This is gonna hurt even worse.


00:41:29.092 --> 00:41:32.462
Connor, find me something
to soak up the blood. Now, now, now.


00:41:33.025 --> 00:41:35.093
Well, Susan isn't gonna believe this.


00:41:36.424 --> 00:41:38.692
l mean, ''What did you do today?''


00:41:40.658 --> 00:41:42.226
''l hunted a crocodile.''


00:41:43.958 --> 00:41:45.159
You're all worked up over this, aren't you?


00:41:45.691 --> 00:41:46.725
Yeah.


00:41:49.157 --> 00:41:51.125
Okay. Here.


00:41:54.724 --> 00:41:55.791
l'm sorry.


00:41:56.925 --> 00:42:00.995
Okay. Connor, start talking.


00:42:01.691 --> 00:42:03.192
l just wanted a pet.


00:42:03.424 --> 00:42:04.625
Sweetie, what was it?


00:42:10.991 --> 00:42:12.058
Mom!


00:42:18.825 --> 00:42:19.825
Hey, Suze, guess what?


00:42:20.124 --> 00:42:21.191
Vica...


00:42:21.291 --> 00:42:22.892
-You there?
-We don't know what...


00:42:23.558 --> 00:42:24.725
-Can you hear me?
-Okay, Susan,


00:42:25.191 --> 00:42:26.759
try to speak a little more slowly


00:42:26.858 --> 00:42:28.226
-and calm down.
-...at the cabin.


00:42:28.458 --> 00:42:30.126
She's at the cabin. She's terrified.


00:42:30.224 --> 00:42:33.193
-And... And l don't know what...
-Okay. Hey...


00:42:35.558 --> 00:42:37.159
Come on. Let's load the guns.


00:42:46.058 --> 00:42:48.660
lt's not that l didn't wanna let
the poor bastard live,


00:42:48.758 --> 00:42:52.528
it's just, how many times do you get
to shoot a giraffe?


00:42:54.025 --> 00:42:55.793
-Hey.
-Anyway, the zoo


00:42:56.291 --> 00:43:00.428
demoted me to the souvenir shop after that.
Can you imagine?


00:43:01.624 --> 00:43:02.925
You're joking, right?


00:43:03.591 --> 00:43:05.359
You shot an animal in captivity?


00:43:05.458 --> 00:43:08.260
Just further proving
that my philosophy is correct.


00:43:08.991 --> 00:43:13.261
Hunting's not fair,
so there's no point in pretending otherwise.


00:43:16.925 --> 00:43:18.359
What's that?


00:43:18.458 --> 00:43:23.362
This is what guarantees you a shot
at the big game.


00:43:25.324 --> 00:43:28.026
Big game is what you're after. Right, Brett?


00:43:30.157 --> 00:43:32.993
Nothing like shooting and eating an animal
you're not supposed to.


00:43:35.524 --> 00:43:37.025
Stop the boat.


00:43:37.391 --> 00:43:40.127
l usually don't take orders,
but l'll let that one slide.


00:43:41.058 --> 00:43:42.659
What'd you see, college boy, a turtle?


00:43:42.891 --> 00:43:43.925
Quiet.


00:43:44.058 --> 00:43:49.029
Okay, that one l'm not gonna let slide.
That's gonna cost you an extra 20.


00:44:02.524 --> 00:44:04.859
What did you see?
Did you see Vica get bitten?


00:44:04.958 --> 00:44:06.359
-No.
-Then whose blood is this?


00:44:07.825 --> 00:44:08.892
Teddy's.


00:44:09.724 --> 00:44:10.791
He went too close to the water


00:44:10.891 --> 00:44:14.160
and l tried calling him
and he wouldn't listen.


00:44:17.958 --> 00:44:18.992
Mom?


00:44:19.791 --> 00:44:20.858
Yeah?


00:44:21.524 --> 00:44:22.691
l fed them.


00:44:23.958 --> 00:44:24.958
What?


00:44:26.925 --> 00:44:28.559
The meat from our freezer.


00:44:28.658 --> 00:44:32.028
And that's why l stole from the store,
because l couldn't feed them enough.


00:44:33.025 --> 00:44:35.293
That's why they ate Vica's dog.


00:44:35.524 --> 00:44:36.558
Connor,


00:44:38.424 --> 00:44:40.292
you've been coming here,
when we told you not to?


00:44:40.825 --> 00:44:41.926
On my bike.


00:44:42.658 --> 00:44:44.326
You knew there were dangerous animals
in the lake


00:44:44.424 --> 00:44:46.759
-and you didn't tell us?
-You would have made Dad kill them.


00:44:48.025 --> 00:44:51.528
Oh, my God. No, no, sweetie, he would...
He would never have done that.


00:44:51.624 --> 00:44:53.125
He would have moved them


00:44:53.224 --> 00:44:55.492
and taken them someplace safe.


00:44:59.058 --> 00:45:00.058
ls she going to be okay?


00:45:02.324 --> 00:45:04.626
l don't know, sweetie. l...


00:45:05.991 --> 00:45:08.393
Try the phone again, please.


00:45:12.958 --> 00:45:16.461
Okay. Okay, Connor,


00:45:18.524 --> 00:45:19.992
we have to get Vica into the car


00:45:20.825 --> 00:45:22.760
and get her to the hospital. Okay?


00:45:23.624 --> 00:45:25.525
Yeah, but what if they come back?


00:45:40.025 --> 00:45:43.094
Doesn't all this take
some of the fun out of it?


00:45:46.391 --> 00:45:48.559
You know what? You're right.


00:45:49.458 --> 00:45:50.892
l think that actually,


00:45:50.991 --> 00:45:54.694
we should track their footprints
and sniff the ground


00:45:54.791 --> 00:45:57.393
to see where they mark their territory.


00:45:59.891 --> 00:46:01.659
All right, guys, close enough.


00:46:01.758 --> 00:46:04.360
We'll let your predator instincts
take over from here, okay?


00:46:04.458 --> 00:46:05.759
-Yep.
-All right.


00:46:07.524 --> 00:46:09.859
This is the fun part.


00:46:28.591 --> 00:46:31.327
Walt! Walt! Walt!


00:46:55.424 --> 00:46:58.593
No. No. Get off of me.


00:47:01.257 --> 00:47:03.192
-Hurry up.
-There's a crocodile.


00:47:03.291 --> 00:47:05.126
-Walt!
-Come on, get her here.


00:47:10.191 --> 00:47:13.694
No. Get off of me. Get off of me. Walt!


00:47:13.791 --> 00:47:15.259
No, don't be an idiot.


00:47:16.324 --> 00:47:17.558
Now get off!


00:47:20.658 --> 00:47:25.596
Damn it. That ain't right.
That ain't anything close to right.


00:47:25.691 --> 00:47:27.359
We need to get the hell out of here.


00:47:27.458 --> 00:47:29.726
Yeah? To where?


00:47:29.825 --> 00:47:31.193
Hey, you're the guide, you tell me.


00:47:39.291 --> 00:47:41.960
-No. No. We can't just leave Walt.
-Of course we can.


00:47:43.025 --> 00:47:45.026
Something just ripped him
to pieces back there.


00:47:45.124 --> 00:47:48.760
But l know, let's all get back in the water.
You grab an arm, you grab a leg


00:47:48.858 --> 00:47:51.293
-and l'll just bring up the rear.
-Shut up.


00:47:51.991 --> 00:47:52.958
Shut up?


00:47:54.558 --> 00:47:56.760
-Shut up? Shut up?
-Just calm down. Relax.


00:47:56.858 --> 00:47:58.025
-Come on.
-You shut up!


00:47:58.124 --> 00:47:59.325
Hey!


00:48:06.424 --> 00:48:07.424
Charlie?


00:48:07.825 --> 00:48:12.196
Hey, man, Tara needs you.
Somebody needs to check her for ticks.


00:48:18.858 --> 00:48:21.327
Okay, Charlie. Enough's enough.


00:48:21.791 --> 00:48:24.193
This isn't funny anymore.
Get your ass back here.


00:48:24.291 --> 00:48:26.660
God. Which direction did he go?


00:48:27.591 --> 00:48:30.961
Knowing Charlie, he's probably finding
a quiet spot to whack off.


00:48:31.624 --> 00:48:34.259
Why did we have to bring him?
He gives me the creeps.


00:48:34.391 --> 00:48:36.493
We shouldn't have brought either of them.


00:48:36.591 --> 00:48:40.294
lt would have given us a chance to be alone
and get to know each other better.


00:48:41.291 --> 00:48:43.559
So, that's what this is about, huh?


00:48:43.958 --> 00:48:45.559
l thought it was pretty obvious.


00:48:47.691 --> 00:48:49.859
You know, the first time l met you,


00:48:51.191 --> 00:48:53.893
well, you had me after hello.


00:48:55.858 --> 00:48:59.094
Look, let's find Charlie first, okay?


00:48:59.524 --> 00:49:02.159
Then we can talk
about what other movie lines you know.


00:49:04.092 --> 00:49:08.362
First you said you didn't like it out here,
and then it was too cold,


00:49:08.458 --> 00:49:11.160
now you wanna waste your time
Iooking for Charlie goofball.


00:49:11.257 --> 00:49:14.026
You certainly bitch and moan a lot.
You know, l thought you'd be grateful


00:49:14.124 --> 00:49:16.025
l asked you along,
considering the alternative.


00:49:26.224 --> 00:49:28.125
You guys?


00:49:28.458 --> 00:49:31.060
Charlie, is that you?


00:49:41.157 --> 00:49:43.125
Mail order piece of crap.


00:49:44.491 --> 00:49:45.758
lt doesn't work.


00:49:51.624 --> 00:49:54.026
Here, this is for you.


00:49:58.092 --> 00:50:00.194
This has got explosive shells in it.


00:50:02.124 --> 00:50:05.360
And this, this is a shark stick.


00:50:06.025 --> 00:50:08.927
Works like a shotgun, but under water.


00:50:09.058 --> 00:50:11.927
One shot from this
will take the head right off a great white.


00:50:12.591 --> 00:50:15.427
You're not a tranquilizer dart
sort of guy, are you?


00:50:16.825 --> 00:50:18.493
Damn straight.


00:50:18.591 --> 00:50:23.996
lf we run into this mythical ''crocodile''
of yours, let's get one thing straight.


00:50:24.092 --> 00:50:27.595
l don't want any of your EPA,
endangered species crap.


00:50:27.691 --> 00:50:29.426
-Are we on the same page?
-Yeah.


00:50:31.624 --> 00:50:34.727
God, Charlie. If you wanna be
a Peeping Tom, l'll save you the trouble.


00:50:36.658 --> 00:50:41.829
What the... Ellie, Aaron!
There's another one of those deer things.


00:50:53.491 --> 00:50:54.692
What's that?


00:50:56.724 --> 00:50:57.958
Where'd it come from?


00:51:00.591 --> 00:51:02.125
l'm not even sure l heard it.


00:51:05.291 --> 00:51:06.592
Ellie.


00:51:11.124 --> 00:51:13.125
So, what do you think did this?


00:51:13.925 --> 00:51:15.192
l bet it was a shark.


00:51:17.958 --> 00:51:19.292
A big shark, a Megalodon.


00:51:20.191 --> 00:51:23.227
A megalo-what?
What the hell have you been smoking?


00:51:23.858 --> 00:51:25.826
That's Charlie Burman,
he's a college student.


00:51:25.925 --> 00:51:30.329
He's here on a backpacking trip.
He's friends with this guy l know.


00:51:31.558 --> 00:51:34.360
l came out here to find my girlfriend
to stop her from doing something stupid.


00:51:36.191 --> 00:51:39.761
Yeah, well, it seems like coming out here
was already pretty stupid.


00:51:42.891 --> 00:51:44.692
Sorry about your friend.


00:51:45.257 --> 00:51:49.527
l hated him. He's an idiot and a pervert.


00:51:50.825 --> 00:51:54.295
Yeah? Then l'm sorry he smells so bad.


00:52:10.058 --> 00:52:11.325
So, what do we do now?


00:52:11.925 --> 00:52:14.093
ln your case, l'd finish high school.


00:52:14.191 --> 00:52:16.893
Until then, get back to the lake
and find our guns.


00:52:18.524 --> 00:52:19.758
They're back.


00:52:20.257 --> 00:52:23.994
Connor, come away from the window.
They can smell you through the glass.


00:52:24.092 --> 00:52:26.727
-ls that true?
-l don't know, honey. Just...


00:52:38.825 --> 00:52:40.026
-Connor.
-Dad!


00:52:43.758 --> 00:52:44.892
Nathan!


00:52:45.291 --> 00:52:47.693
Susan, stay away from the window!


00:52:49.157 --> 00:52:51.058
The bathroom.
There's thick walls in the bathroom.


00:52:51.157 --> 00:52:52.358
Help me with Vica.


00:52:56.891 --> 00:52:58.692
Let them get closer.


00:53:00.758 --> 00:53:02.759
Lay down. Here you go.


00:53:05.491 --> 00:53:06.491
Five,


00:53:08.925 --> 00:53:12.094
four, three...


00:53:12.191 --> 00:53:13.825
Down, honey. Down.


00:53:14.691 --> 00:53:17.393
...two, one.


00:53:40.558 --> 00:53:42.760
Honey, it's fine. Stay here, okay?


00:53:42.858 --> 00:53:44.159
-But, Mom...
-Connor!


00:54:09.224 --> 00:54:10.858
Oh, my God.


00:54:40.925 --> 00:54:43.794
-Nathan!
-Hey, you okay?


00:54:45.458 --> 00:54:47.726
-Where's Connor?
-Dad!


00:54:47.825 --> 00:54:50.160
-Connor! Hey, you okay?
-Yeah.


00:55:27.858 --> 00:55:29.960
-Tony?
-Open up.


00:55:37.591 --> 00:55:39.960
l officially owe you an apology.


00:55:43.291 --> 00:55:46.694
Great. Now she's gone.
Where the hell is she?


00:55:47.092 --> 00:55:48.359
Tara!


00:55:49.858 --> 00:55:53.228
No. No. No! No!


00:55:54.825 --> 00:55:57.060
She was... She was...


00:55:58.324 --> 00:56:02.428
lt's okay. It's okay. Come on. Come on.
It's okay. It's okay.


00:56:02.524 --> 00:56:05.760
Don't worry. Don't worry.
It's going to be okay.


00:56:15.858 --> 00:56:17.459
Could be a gator.


00:56:21.524 --> 00:56:26.061
l'm sure she's fine,
this damsel in distress of yours.


00:56:27.424 --> 00:56:31.995
This is about another guy. Yeah.
She goes on a camping trip without you,


00:56:32.092 --> 00:56:37.163
so you hire a hunting guide
to help you stalk her through a state forest.


00:56:37.257 --> 00:56:38.458
Totally normal.


00:56:41.257 --> 00:56:43.425
For a complete jealous psycho.


00:56:44.524 --> 00:56:46.392
What she do,
forget her chastity belt at home?


00:56:47.424 --> 00:56:51.027
lt's a little more complicated than that,
and it's not your damn problem.


00:56:51.925 --> 00:56:53.192
Not my problem?


00:56:53.291 --> 00:56:57.695
Hey, getting you all back in one piece
is my responsibility,


00:56:57.858 --> 00:57:00.694
and l take it very seriously,
thank you very much.


00:57:01.257 --> 00:57:03.359
So the least you could do


00:57:03.458 --> 00:57:07.762
is drop your ''l got a stick
up my college educated butt'' attitude.


00:57:10.825 --> 00:57:13.928
Yes, she came with another guy.


00:57:18.092 --> 00:57:19.526
Damn, l'm good.


00:57:23.025 --> 00:57:26.862
Hey, now guess what l found.


00:57:31.391 --> 00:57:36.429
Now, before we all got unceremoniously
jacked from my boat,


00:57:36.624 --> 00:57:39.393
we were following a tracking signal
from an elk.


00:57:39.491 --> 00:57:41.326
Now that elk, it seems, is actually


00:57:41.424 --> 00:57:44.927
passing through the digestive tract
of our gator friend.


00:57:48.524 --> 00:57:51.827
l'm sorry to put it this way,
but predators go to where their food is.


00:57:51.925 --> 00:57:55.895
So whatever killed smelly over there
knows where your girlfriend is.


00:57:55.991 --> 00:57:58.393
Now, all we have to do is follow him. Okay?


00:58:01.191 --> 00:58:04.160
Come on, baby. Come on, talk to Mama.


00:58:06.224 --> 00:58:07.491
Yes.


00:58:10.891 --> 00:58:13.960
We could go to that guy's cabin
across the lake, try to find some help.


00:58:14.058 --> 00:58:15.058
Relax.


00:58:15.157 --> 00:58:17.325
That guy who works for the state,
he'd know who to call.


00:58:17.424 --> 00:58:19.959
We don't need any help, l can handle this.


00:58:22.591 --> 00:58:25.694
lsn't this what you wanted?
A bit of time away from the world?


00:58:25.791 --> 00:58:30.829
l wanted to forget about Brett for a few days.
Not get lost in the Land of the Lost.


00:58:31.691 --> 00:58:34.994
Hell, at least if Brett was here,
he wouldn't give up on finding his friends.


00:58:35.092 --> 00:58:36.860
Well, you seem to have forgotten
about him all right.


00:58:38.257 --> 00:58:42.928
Look, l'm just trying to help. That's all.


00:58:46.791 --> 00:58:52.196
Seriously? My best friend is missing.
We need to get help.


00:59:15.124 --> 00:59:16.358
Nothing bigger than a trout?


00:59:21.357 --> 00:59:24.560
l'd say that thing's
a little bigger than a goddamn trout!


00:59:26.458 --> 00:59:31.062
l know this is just a job for you,
but everyone l have left is in this room,


00:59:31.157 --> 00:59:34.460
and they're in danger because l trusted you.


00:59:35.958 --> 00:59:37.526
lt's gotta be 25 feet long.


00:59:38.191 --> 00:59:41.460
l screwed up. Is that what you wanna hear?
l'm sorry.


00:59:41.558 --> 00:59:45.228
The big one, l have no idea.
It could have been dropped from the sky.


00:59:45.324 --> 00:59:46.758
Yeah, dropped from...


00:59:53.257 --> 00:59:54.324
The elk.


00:59:57.092 --> 01:00:00.662
Three years ago, the EPA re-introduced elk
just down the river.


01:00:01.092 --> 01:00:03.160
Predators move towards their food.


01:00:04.758 --> 01:00:09.696
lt is possible that it didn't show up
on your sonar because it wasn't in the lake.


01:00:10.324 --> 01:00:12.926
Question is, why'd they come back here?


01:00:13.025 --> 01:00:14.025
l don't...


01:00:14.124 --> 01:00:16.192
l mean, did the big one follow the elk
into the area?


01:00:16.291 --> 01:00:17.258
l don't know.


01:00:18.591 --> 01:00:22.661
lt's an answer for the big one,
but the smaller ones,


01:00:22.758 --> 01:00:26.294
they've been here for months.
Talk to your son.


01:00:34.157 --> 01:00:38.361
Hey, l'm gonna go check and see
what kind of shampoo you use.


01:00:45.058 --> 01:00:46.793
You knew about them?


01:00:56.591 --> 01:00:58.359
Come here. Come here.


01:01:00.092 --> 01:01:02.594
ls this where you've been going
on your bike every day?


01:01:03.458 --> 01:01:07.195
You know, they almost killed Vica?
You know they can kill you?


01:01:07.491 --> 01:01:12.229
-Never hurt me.
-Listen! They're not your friends.


01:01:12.791 --> 01:01:17.295
They're wild animals. And wild animals
live by a set of rules to ensure their survival.


01:01:17.391 --> 01:01:20.994
One of the rules is that they eat
anything smaller than they are.


01:01:22.357 --> 01:01:25.660
Do you understand that?
They're not your friends.


01:01:25.758 --> 01:01:29.862
lt was just something cool to play with.
Both of you left me alone.


01:01:30.291 --> 01:01:32.559
You care more about your stupid elk
than me,


01:01:32.658 --> 01:01:34.659
and Mom's always working.


01:01:35.524 --> 01:01:39.427
You know, l thought it was a rule of nature
that parents took care of their kids.


01:01:40.324 --> 01:01:41.758
My mistake.


01:02:01.958 --> 01:02:02.925
Hey.


01:02:07.724 --> 01:02:11.194
So, still think we can get a good price
for this place?


01:02:19.825 --> 01:02:25.230
lt's a fixer-upper, real curb-appeal,
pets included.


01:02:26.758 --> 01:02:31.996
Yeah. And l, for one, am ready
to say goodbye to lake-side living forever.


01:02:35.758 --> 01:02:38.293
Sweets, l think we should
make a break for it.


01:02:38.391 --> 01:02:40.392
l don't think Vica's gonna make it if we wait


01:02:40.491 --> 01:02:42.559
and we still have a couple hours
of daylight left.


01:02:42.658 --> 01:02:45.160
-Yeah, but she can't walk.
-We can carry her.


01:02:48.224 --> 01:02:49.458
l know you're scared.


01:02:50.524 --> 01:02:55.762
But with Willinger covering us,
we should be able to make it.


01:02:59.458 --> 01:03:00.525
Okay.


01:03:01.491 --> 01:03:02.458
You sure?


01:03:08.658 --> 01:03:11.861
We're gonna have to get the car close
if we're gonna get everyone inside.


01:03:11.958 --> 01:03:13.959
-All right.
-Okay.


01:03:15.025 --> 01:03:19.062
Connor, take care of your mother. Okay?


01:03:19.724 --> 01:03:21.358
-Okay.
-Okay.


01:03:26.124 --> 01:03:27.959
Looks like
we're actually gonna do this thing.


01:03:28.191 --> 01:03:29.225
l love you.


01:03:39.424 --> 01:03:40.691
-lf something happens...
-lt won't.


01:03:42.191 --> 01:03:45.227
But if it does, l'll keep Connor safe, okay?


01:03:45.858 --> 01:03:48.527
Well, l was gonna say, ''Come save us.''


01:04:05.157 --> 01:04:06.157
Let's do this.


01:04:20.591 --> 01:04:22.459
Come on, come on. Come on, come on.


01:04:22.558 --> 01:04:23.525
Go.


01:04:26.758 --> 01:04:28.292
-Let's go!
-l'm trying!


01:04:52.124 --> 01:04:53.291
That one's new!


01:04:55.357 --> 01:04:58.493
Mom, Mom, what are you doing?


01:04:58.591 --> 01:05:00.225
Connor, stay here. l mean it.


01:05:03.025 --> 01:05:05.894
-Mom, you have to press the red button.
-What?


01:05:10.224 --> 01:05:12.559
-How do you know that stuff?
-lt's always the red button.


01:05:13.458 --> 01:05:14.425
Mom!


01:05:18.124 --> 01:05:20.192
Susan, get back in the house.


01:05:25.357 --> 01:05:26.524
Susan!


01:05:34.724 --> 01:05:35.724
Mom!


01:05:42.257 --> 01:05:44.492
Hey! Get away from her.


01:05:47.491 --> 01:05:48.592
Come on.


01:05:54.491 --> 01:05:56.025
No, no, no, no, no.


01:06:16.257 --> 01:06:18.292
Susan, get to the cabin!


01:06:22.058 --> 01:06:23.092
Go now! Go!


01:06:33.624 --> 01:06:34.658
lt's locked!


01:06:38.424 --> 01:06:40.459
-Vica!
-Vica, open the door.


01:06:40.558 --> 01:06:42.326
-Vica!
-Vica!


01:06:43.424 --> 01:06:44.725
Open the door!


01:06:58.858 --> 01:07:01.293
Go, go. Back there.


01:07:01.391 --> 01:07:03.860
-l wanna help!
-Now, Connor!


01:07:06.791 --> 01:07:09.193
Vica! Vica!


01:07:10.791 --> 01:07:12.192
He's coming through.


01:07:34.092 --> 01:07:36.627
You got us turned around.
l don't even know which way camp was.


01:07:36.724 --> 01:07:38.859
l heard a noise towards this way.


01:07:38.958 --> 01:07:41.794
You heard gunshots.
Do we really wanna go towards gunshots?


01:07:41.891 --> 01:07:44.226
We wanna go towards...


01:07:48.925 --> 01:07:50.893
Oh, my God!


01:07:51.658 --> 01:07:55.094
Oh, my God. We need to get the hell
away from here. Now!


01:07:55.191 --> 01:07:56.926
-Tara!
-Who the hell cares about Tara?


01:07:57.025 --> 01:07:58.359
-Get up. Don't cry. Come on.
-l can't.


01:07:58.458 --> 01:08:00.426
-l can't.
-l'm not gonna say it again.


01:08:00.524 --> 01:08:03.760
Get up, damn it.
Stop being a little bitch and get up.


01:08:05.357 --> 01:08:07.659
Look, l'm going this way
with or without you.


01:08:09.191 --> 01:08:11.459
-Look, it's Brett's jacket. Brett's jacket.
-What, are you crazy?


01:08:11.558 --> 01:08:13.927
l don't know what the hell is going on here,
but we need to leave.


01:08:14.025 --> 01:08:15.292
l think he's looking for me.


01:08:17.058 --> 01:08:21.495
You can't be serious.
You think Brett gives a rat's ass about you?


01:08:21.591 --> 01:08:24.293
You think he cares enough about you
to get his shoes dirty?


01:08:24.391 --> 01:08:27.527
lf that were true, you wouldn't be here
with me in the first place.


01:08:27.624 --> 01:08:31.361
He's cheating on you, Ellie,
and everybody at school knows it but you.


01:08:32.958 --> 01:08:36.261
No, no, no, no.
Maybe he heard the gunshots.


01:08:36.357 --> 01:08:38.225
Or maybe, maybe he fired them.


01:08:38.324 --> 01:08:41.126
Why do you put him on such a pedestal?


01:08:41.224 --> 01:08:44.493
He doesn't give a rat's ass about you,
he told me so himself.


01:08:46.191 --> 01:08:48.092
He's not out looking for you.


01:08:48.191 --> 01:08:52.194
He's back at school, probably
in some freshman's dorm room right now.


01:08:52.624 --> 01:08:54.225
We got a camp a few miles away from here.


01:08:54.324 --> 01:08:56.693
We find the camp
and we can find our way home.


01:08:58.191 --> 01:09:00.893
No, no.
We've been turned around for an hour now.


01:09:00.991 --> 01:09:03.960
The only way we know
is towards the gunshots.


01:09:04.058 --> 01:09:09.663
Make your choice. Let someone who really
cares about you save you,


01:09:10.991 --> 01:09:13.993
or you can go crying to Brett like usual.


01:09:16.691 --> 01:09:20.327
No. Please, please don't leave me.


01:09:20.424 --> 01:09:23.326
You go in that direction
and you're walking alone.


01:09:23.424 --> 01:09:24.958
Please come with me.


01:09:26.691 --> 01:09:28.659
Aaron! Aaron.


01:09:53.858 --> 01:09:56.594
This is actually the most fun
l've had in quite a while.


01:09:57.891 --> 01:10:00.693
Some fun. l can't tell if l'm excited,


01:10:00.791 --> 01:10:02.726
or if l'm going to throw up in my mouth
from the terror.


01:10:05.925 --> 01:10:08.460
-Just in case it's the latter.
-All right.


01:10:13.724 --> 01:10:15.258
We don't even know
what the hell this thing is yet,


01:10:15.357 --> 01:10:18.393
and l'm already picking out
a spot on my wall for its head.


01:10:19.524 --> 01:10:23.194
You know what?
Maybe it's mutating and has two heads.


01:10:23.891 --> 01:10:26.093
lf that happens to be the case,
l get them both.


01:10:26.191 --> 01:10:28.059
lf there's three heads, you can have one.


01:10:28.157 --> 01:10:30.459
Guys, l can hear you. My girlfriend?


01:10:30.758 --> 01:10:33.861
You know, if he wants one of the heads,
l'm not giving him one of mine.


01:10:33.958 --> 01:10:35.292
He can't have mine neither.


01:10:35.391 --> 01:10:37.493
l didn't come out here to fight wild animals.


01:10:37.591 --> 01:10:41.194
Hey, hey, you know what? Look, we can't
find your girlfriend if we're all gator crap.


01:10:42.424 --> 01:10:47.028
Last chance, Brett. You gonna tell us
why you're stalking your own girlfriend?


01:10:47.124 --> 01:10:48.458
Wait a minute.


01:10:48.558 --> 01:10:51.594
lf this is about a restraining order,
there are ways around that.


01:10:51.691 --> 01:10:53.692
Believe me, l know.


01:10:53.925 --> 01:10:56.560
She's being lied to, about me.


01:10:58.825 --> 01:11:02.995
There's this guy, Aaron. He's a grad student.
He was tutoring her for a while.


01:11:03.124 --> 01:11:06.360
He told her there was another girl and
he used that opportunity to get between us.


01:11:06.458 --> 01:11:08.326
And now, he takes her with him on this trip


01:11:08.424 --> 01:11:09.892
and you can only guess
what he's hoping to do with her.


01:11:10.357 --> 01:11:11.691
l love it out here.


01:11:13.124 --> 01:11:14.859
Where's Dr. Phil when you need him?


01:11:18.825 --> 01:11:20.193
Who's Dr. Phil?


01:11:36.092 --> 01:11:37.259
lt's not her.


01:11:42.491 --> 01:11:43.625
Oh, my God. It's Tara.


01:11:43.724 --> 01:11:46.393
-Brett, get back.
-lt's her best friend. She must be close.


01:11:46.491 --> 01:11:50.027
We gotta find her. Ellie! Can you hear me?


01:11:50.124 --> 01:11:51.225
Shut up.


01:11:51.324 --> 01:11:52.892
Well, that's one way to bring them closer.


01:11:52.991 --> 01:11:54.659
Can you hear me?


01:11:54.758 --> 01:11:57.293
Shut up! Jonas, you ready for this?


01:11:59.124 --> 01:12:00.992
-Try not to mess up its head.
-Heads.


01:12:01.092 --> 01:12:02.226
Ellie!


01:12:26.758 --> 01:12:29.861
Man, that's gotta be the hottest thing
l've ever seen.


01:12:51.124 --> 01:12:52.091
Shit.


01:12:53.958 --> 01:12:55.225
He's awake.


01:12:59.291 --> 01:13:00.959
-All right, get Connor ready to run.
-Right.


01:13:10.357 --> 01:13:12.559
Need a bigger gun.
Definitely need a bigger gun.


01:13:13.991 --> 01:13:14.958
Wait!


01:13:16.058 --> 01:13:17.025
Stop!


01:14:16.991 --> 01:14:18.258
What was l thinking?


01:14:18.357 --> 01:14:19.891
Give me that.


01:14:22.291 --> 01:14:26.595
l'm afraid that l have to ban you
from ever participating


01:14:26.691 --> 01:14:30.061
in one of my hunting expeditions,
ever again.


01:14:30.157 --> 01:14:33.293
Something in the contract
about not blowing holes in the guide.


01:14:33.391 --> 01:14:35.593
No complaints from me.


01:14:35.691 --> 01:14:39.294
That bastard ruined my pants
and he stole my knife.


01:14:39.591 --> 01:14:41.793
Well, you stabbed him in the face.


01:14:42.357 --> 01:14:46.060
Yeah, l know. And l would have
carved my name in his hide


01:14:46.157 --> 01:14:47.992
had it not got stuck in his head.


01:14:48.424 --> 01:14:49.825
As for your bellyaching,


01:14:50.858 --> 01:14:53.994
it's not the first time
l've been shot by someone l know.


01:14:54.092 --> 01:14:56.427
God! It is the first time l've been hit.


01:15:03.991 --> 01:15:06.793
l'm afraid l'm not going to be able
to walk out of here.


01:15:11.925 --> 01:15:12.925
The boat.


01:15:14.858 --> 01:15:20.296
The boat? Yeah. Getting in the water
sounds like a fine idea to me, college boy.


01:15:20.524 --> 01:15:22.492
Well, unless you can think of another way.


01:15:22.591 --> 01:15:25.160
Actually, no, l can't.


01:15:25.858 --> 01:15:28.594
No way to keep our orientation
with the sun going down.


01:15:28.691 --> 01:15:31.393
When we get in the boat, where do we go?


01:15:32.025 --> 01:15:33.793
Only one place to go.


01:15:35.858 --> 01:15:38.727
There's a cabin on the other side of the lake.


01:15:40.157 --> 01:15:44.294
l'm having a bit of a misunderstanding
with the owner,


01:15:44.391 --> 01:15:49.829
so if anybody's there when we get there,
just keep the elk poaching on the down low.


01:15:55.291 --> 01:15:58.861
l'm the one with the injured leg,
Rambo, okay? Let's go.


01:15:58.958 --> 01:16:00.025
What about Ellie?


01:16:01.224 --> 01:16:04.694
We can't... We can't go looking for her now.
We wouldn't know where to look.


01:16:04.791 --> 01:16:08.094
-You think she's dead, don't you?
-l didn't say that.


01:16:09.025 --> 01:16:11.527
Look, l can't know for sure,


01:16:11.624 --> 01:16:14.793
but we wouldn't do her any good
if we get ourselves killed, would we?


01:16:14.891 --> 01:16:17.893
Those were crocodiles.
l've read enough about crocodiles


01:16:17.991 --> 01:16:20.893
to know they don't stop killing food
just because they're full.


01:16:21.324 --> 01:16:23.826
They also don't travel very far
if they don't have to. She's nearby.


01:16:23.925 --> 01:16:28.963
Whatever you do, do not start screaming
like you did the last time.


01:16:29.058 --> 01:16:30.759
She's my girlfriend!


01:16:30.858 --> 01:16:33.093
lf you had any kind of normal relationships,
you'd understand.


01:16:33.724 --> 01:16:35.025
Normal?


01:16:36.391 --> 01:16:42.663
Jonas and l chase
after a killer crocodile for you,


01:16:42.758 --> 01:16:45.060
practically playing 20 questions


01:16:45.157 --> 01:16:49.528
trying to figure out what would drive you
to follow Ellie in here to begin with.


01:16:49.624 --> 01:16:53.894
And may l point out that we didn't
even know the damsel's name


01:16:53.991 --> 01:16:57.260
until you start screaming it
at the top of your lungs,


01:16:57.357 --> 01:17:01.527
attracting that monster that came out
of the woods and bit off Jonas' head.


01:17:03.291 --> 01:17:06.761
And how the hell do you know
l don't have any normal relationships, huh?


01:17:06.858 --> 01:17:10.795
l know all about you.
All about your boo-hooing about Miss Ellie,


01:17:10.958 --> 01:17:14.294
but did you ask me one question,
one question about me and my life?


01:17:14.391 --> 01:17:15.525
Okay!


01:17:18.891 --> 01:17:19.891
Do you have a boyfriend?


01:17:22.691 --> 01:17:26.494
No. No, l don't have a boyfriend, dumbass.


01:17:27.357 --> 01:17:28.991
That was hypothetical.


01:17:30.058 --> 01:17:35.663
Now that you know all about me,
Iet's get in the boat and go someplace safe.


01:17:37.025 --> 01:17:38.259
No, l won't.


01:17:38.357 --> 01:17:40.025
-Really?
-Not without Ellie.


01:17:47.157 --> 01:17:50.493
Fine, we'll see how you like being dragged.


01:18:10.324 --> 01:18:12.759
-Johnny Law.
-Nathan, actually.


01:18:13.324 --> 01:18:16.360
l would have introduced myself last time,
but when l asked for your hunter's license


01:18:16.458 --> 01:18:18.326
you spit tobacco juice on my shoes.


01:18:18.424 --> 01:18:21.059
Yeah? l'm a shy girl.


01:18:22.758 --> 01:18:28.430
You know, you got a bit of an infestation
of a very unusual variety out there.


01:18:29.658 --> 01:18:31.493
Yeah, it looks like they got you pretty bad.


01:18:31.591 --> 01:18:34.060
There were four of us. And the other two


01:18:36.858 --> 01:18:41.195
didn't fare as well.


01:18:42.025 --> 01:18:43.693
But the crocs didn't shoot me.


01:18:46.524 --> 01:18:49.326
-That one did.
-l already said l was sorry.


01:18:51.157 --> 01:18:53.959
Thanks for taking us in,
but we need to get back out there.


01:18:54.058 --> 01:18:55.859
-l'm Brett, by the way.
-Nathan.


01:18:55.958 --> 01:18:57.592
Hey. Susan. This is Connor.


01:18:57.691 --> 01:18:59.626
Why would you wanna go back outside?
Are you crazy?


01:18:59.724 --> 01:19:01.992
Because my girlfriend's out there
on the lake.


01:19:02.458 --> 01:19:05.861
We were looking for her
when Reba decided to come here instead.


01:19:05.958 --> 01:19:09.561
lt's better off behind a closed door
than running around in the dark.


01:19:09.658 --> 01:19:12.427
Exactly why we need to get back on the boat
and find Ellie.


01:19:12.524 --> 01:19:13.725
We've been trapped in here for hours


01:19:13.825 --> 01:19:16.327
and there's the very real possibility
that help isn't coming.


01:19:16.424 --> 01:19:18.159
Now, we can't let you take
our only means of transportation


01:19:18.257 --> 01:19:19.291
and go and get yourself killed.


01:19:19.391 --> 01:19:22.694
Especially when that only means
of transportation belongs to me.


01:19:22.791 --> 01:19:26.494
We get back in the boat. We find Ellie,
and then we get the hell away from here.


01:19:26.591 --> 01:19:28.926
Ellie's on the lake.
Now we need to get to safety.


01:19:29.025 --> 01:19:30.493
That's connecting to the river
and going down to town.


01:19:30.591 --> 01:19:31.658
Those are opposite directions.


01:19:31.758 --> 01:19:34.160
No! This isn't up for debate.
We're not leaving her.


01:19:34.257 --> 01:19:36.459
We don't even know where she is.


01:19:36.558 --> 01:19:38.693
Now my wife and my son are right here
and l can't risk their lives


01:19:38.791 --> 01:19:40.792
based on the chance or the possibility
that she might be out there.


01:19:40.891 --> 01:19:43.893
Sensible conversation
didn't get me very far with her.


01:19:46.658 --> 01:19:47.859
l'm sorry to have to do this.


01:19:51.291 --> 01:19:53.526
l already shot someone today.
l don't mind doing it again.


01:19:53.624 --> 01:19:54.858
Get away from the door.


01:19:55.257 --> 01:19:57.492
Now's a fine time to grow yourself a pair.


01:20:01.858 --> 01:20:05.661
l will come back for you, promise.
Just as soon as l find her.


01:20:22.357 --> 01:20:23.424
Ellie!


01:20:31.958 --> 01:20:33.592
Ellie!


01:20:34.424 --> 01:20:35.491
Brett?


01:20:36.324 --> 01:20:38.359
Ellie!


01:20:43.025 --> 01:20:44.626
Ellie!


01:20:45.891 --> 01:20:47.125
Brett!


01:20:47.491 --> 01:20:48.992
Ellie!


01:20:49.658 --> 01:20:50.792
Brett!


01:20:57.357 --> 01:20:59.292
Be back sooner than l thought.


01:20:59.391 --> 01:21:01.493
Brett! Brett!


01:21:01.724 --> 01:21:03.025
l'm coming back!


01:21:03.157 --> 01:21:05.025
Brett, l'm here!


01:21:05.491 --> 01:21:06.892
Ellie!


01:21:06.991 --> 01:21:11.195
l'm here, baby. l'm here.
l knew. l knew. Brett!


01:21:16.324 --> 01:21:19.660
Connor, get in the bathroom
and lock the door. Go!


01:21:40.458 --> 01:21:41.559
Brett!


01:21:41.658 --> 01:21:42.692
No, no.


01:21:42.791 --> 01:21:45.026
Oh, my God. l knew. l knew.


01:21:45.124 --> 01:21:46.859
Move away from the water!


01:21:47.624 --> 01:21:48.691
What?


01:21:48.791 --> 01:21:52.995
Get away from the water!
Get away from the water!


01:22:19.891 --> 01:22:20.958
Ellie!


01:22:25.591 --> 01:22:26.925
Oh, my God!


01:22:37.958 --> 01:22:39.459
What is that?


01:22:45.257 --> 01:22:46.491
-l'm so sorry.
-Hey...


01:22:46.591 --> 01:22:48.426
Hey, hey. No. You don't need to apologize.


01:22:48.524 --> 01:22:51.293
-l'm sorry for going with him. With Aaron.
-Don't apologize. Don't.


01:22:51.391 --> 01:22:53.292
No. No, don't apologize.


01:22:57.324 --> 01:23:00.760
-l love you. l love you.
-l love you.


01:23:05.791 --> 01:23:08.927
Ellie, go. Go now. Go! Run! Now!


01:23:10.724 --> 01:23:13.860
Oh, my God. What is... What is that?


01:23:19.591 --> 01:23:20.792
Oh, my God!


01:23:44.758 --> 01:23:45.859
Nicely done.


01:23:46.092 --> 01:23:48.527
Let's get the hell out of here, now.


01:23:56.558 --> 01:23:59.894
That's okay.
l can always come back for the head later.


01:24:03.357 --> 01:24:05.025
Connor, stay close.


01:24:09.524 --> 01:24:11.158
Hey, hey, hey, hey.


01:24:12.424 --> 01:24:15.293
-Help me. It killed... It killed him.
-Who? Who?


01:24:15.391 --> 01:24:16.458
-Brett?
-Brett.


01:24:16.558 --> 01:24:19.861
-Get us in the boat, now!
-Right. Go! Go! Connor, come.


01:24:21.124 --> 01:24:22.792
-You okay?
-Yeah.


01:24:27.092 --> 01:24:28.326
Keep trying.


01:24:33.291 --> 01:24:35.359
Okay, plan B.


01:24:43.491 --> 01:24:44.725
Here we go.


01:24:46.424 --> 01:24:47.858
Yeah, l think we're safe.


01:24:48.891 --> 01:24:50.025
What is that?


01:24:53.825 --> 01:24:56.394
Go. Go. Go. Come on. Go.


01:25:03.092 --> 01:25:04.226
Got her?


01:25:07.058 --> 01:25:08.592
-Hello!
-Hello!


01:25:08.691 --> 01:25:09.725
Come on!


01:25:11.058 --> 01:25:12.159
Over there.


01:25:12.257 --> 01:25:15.360
What makes you think Dimitri's
not gonna have locked his doors?


01:25:23.058 --> 01:25:24.125
What now?


01:25:28.025 --> 01:25:29.059
After you.


01:25:37.658 --> 01:25:39.526
-Okay, let's put her down.
-l'll call for help.


01:25:39.624 --> 01:25:40.658
All right.


01:25:41.825 --> 01:25:43.960
-Does anybody have a quarter?
-No. No.


01:25:44.058 --> 01:25:46.527
-lt's 911, you don't need any money.
-Okay, okay.


01:25:59.391 --> 01:26:04.729
No, no, no, no, no. It's going to be okay.
We're gonna get out of here.


01:26:17.724 --> 01:26:21.828
What about Connor? This is all my fault.
l should have been there for him.


01:26:21.925 --> 01:26:23.026
This is my fault.


01:26:39.124 --> 01:26:43.595
lt's you. Little Bickerman! Don't you...


01:26:47.691 --> 01:26:50.326
Oh, my God! Run. Go, go, go!


01:27:27.624 --> 01:27:31.527
Help! Help! Help!


01:27:32.058 --> 01:27:33.325
Help!


01:27:37.891 --> 01:27:40.193
Help! Help!


01:28:05.758 --> 01:28:08.227
Connor! Susan! Backdoor's open. Go!


01:28:25.491 --> 01:28:26.491
No keys.


01:28:26.591 --> 01:28:29.093
-Don't you know how to hot-wire?
-l'm a zoologist.


01:28:29.858 --> 01:28:31.693
-Connor!
-Connor?


01:28:35.524 --> 01:28:36.591
Keys.


01:28:37.825 --> 01:28:40.994
This is the one and only time
you're allowed to steal something.


01:29:11.391 --> 01:29:13.292
Connor. Go.


01:29:29.458 --> 01:29:31.893
-Are we 07 or 08?
-07!


01:29:47.624 --> 01:29:48.958
Connor!


01:29:51.157 --> 01:29:52.925
Dad! Lighter!


01:30:13.291 --> 01:30:15.760
-Nate! Nate!
-No. Dad!


01:30:52.357 --> 01:30:55.993
l would like to present to you today
an absolutely extraordinary case,


01:30:56.524 --> 01:30:59.927
and proof that we are not in control.


01:31:01.624 --> 01:31:06.195
We're not in control of our jobs,
we're not in control of our children


01:31:07.491 --> 01:31:10.727
and we are certainly not in control
of this planet.


01:31:12.558 --> 01:31:14.893
There are no hard and fast rules in nature.


01:31:15.391 --> 01:31:20.162
There's no way to create a system
by which we can catalog and analyze


01:31:20.257 --> 01:31:22.926
and predict where an animal is gonna go


01:31:24.691 --> 01:31:27.193
or what an animal is gonna do.


01:31:28.025 --> 01:31:30.927
Having said all that,
l would like to now regale you


01:31:31.025 --> 01:31:36.663
with the story of a most unique species,
the Maine River Crocodile.


01:31:37.891 --> 01:31:40.727
For the record, it's extinct.


01:31:45.791 --> 01:31:46.858
Come along.


01:31:47.925 --> 01:31:52.195
So, did you guys have time
to read the pamphlets? Anyone?

